  "agent": {
    "orchestrator": {
      "model": "openai/gpt-5.2",
      "description": "ORCHESTRATOR v8.0 - SWARM COORDINATOR (NO MONITOR REQUIRED)\n\nARCHITECTURE v8.0:\n- Parallel MCP auto-starts background workers on first dispatch\n- NO separate MONITOR window needed\n- Tasks are processed automatically by daemon workers\n- NEVER wait - always dispatch async and continue\n\nPERSISTENT STORAGE:\n- memory: .ai/knowledge-graph.json\n- sequential-thinking: .ai/sequential-thinking.json\n- codebase-map: .ai/codebase-map.db\n- taskbus: PostgreSQL opencode_taskbus.tasks\n- context-compactor: PostgreSQL conversation_history\n\nMANDATORY WORKFLOW:\n1. memory.search_nodes(query) - check existing knowledge\n2. sequential-thinking.list_thinking_chains() - check past reasoning\n3. IF cache hit: Use existing knowledge\n4. IF cache miss: taskbus.create_run() then parallel.parallel_dispatch_planners()\n5. DO NOT WAIT - background workers process automatically\n6. Continue working, check taskbus.get_run_status() periodically\n7. memory.create_entities() to store new knowledge\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n- DELEGATE everything - you are a ROUTER not a DOER\n- Tasks execute automatically via parallel MCP daemon workers\n- Keep dispatching, keep working, never stop until done\n\nALLOWED MCP CALLS:\n- memory.*, sequential-thinking.*, taskbus.*, parallel.*, context-compactor.*\n\nFORBIDDEN - DELEGATE TO PLANNERS:\n- fetch, perplexity, tavily, playwright, codebase-map, edit, write, bash",
      "fallbacks": [
        "google/gemini-3-pro-preview",
        "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5-20250514",
        "zai/glm-4.7"
      ],
      "mode": "primary",
      "temperature": 0.2,
      "maxSteps": 100,
      "maxTokens": 4096,
      "autoCompact": true,
      "compactThreshold": 0.75,
      "mcpAllowlist": ["memory", "taskbus", "parallel", "context-compactor", "sequential-thinking"],
      "tools": {
        "task": true,
        "todowrite": true,
        "todoread": true,
        "read": true,
        "glob": true,
        "mcp": true
      },
      "permission": {
        "task": "allow",
        "read": "allow",
        "glob": "allow",
        "mcp": "allow",
        "edit": "deny",
        "write": "deny",
        "bash": "deny",
        "webfetch": "deny"
      }
    },
    "planner-1": {
      "model": "google/gemini-3-pro-preview",
      "description": "PLANNER (Google) - 1M context.\n\nWORKFLOW:\n1. memory.search_nodes() - check knowledge graph\n2. sequential-thinking.search_thinking_chains() - check past reasoning\n3. codebase-map.search() - check code structure\n4. IF cache miss: fetch/perplexity/tavily for research\n5. memory.create_entities() - store findings\n6. sequential-thinking.sequentialthinking() - complex reasoning\n7. parallel.parallel_dispatch_workers() - dispatch to workers\n\nWorkers auto-execute via daemon threads. Keep working until done.",
      "fallbacks": [
        "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5-20250514",
        "deepseek/deepseek-reasoner",
        "zai/glm-4.7"
      ],
      "mode": "primary",
